      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:5:33:10",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ الصَّادِقَ ( عليه السلام ) أَدْفَعُ عُشْرَ مَالِي إِلَى وُلْدِ ابْنَتِي قَالَ نَعَمْ لَا بَأْسَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Idrees, and someone else, from Muhammad Bin Ahmad, from one of our companions, from Muhammad Bin Jazzaki who said, ",
          "‘I asked Al-Sadiq<sup>asws</sup>, ‘Can I hand over the tax (10%) of my wealth to the children of my daughter?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes, and there is no problem’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "10. Ahmad ibn Idris and others have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from certain persons of our people from Muhammad ibn Jazzak who has said the following: “I once asked al-Sadiq, abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, ‘Can I give one out of ten of my asset to the children of my daughter? He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, it is not harmful.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
